# ── Env & secrets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ⚠ THE PATTERN IS `.env.*`, NOT A LIST, AND THAT IS AV7-AUD-F5's FIRST FIX.
# This block used to read `.env` / `.env.local` / `.env.*.local`, which left
# `.env.production`, `.env.test` and `.env.development` COMMITTABLE — measured:
#   NOT IGNORED (committable): .env.test / .env.development / .env.production
# That mattered because `apps/web/next.config.ts` calls
# `loadEnvConfig(repoRoot, NODE_ENV !== 'production')`, so Next reads
# `.env.production` on every `next start` — and a committed one satisfied BOTH
# conditions of the fail-closed auth rate-limit override on the very process
# that serves `/api/auth/*`, with a `console.warn` as the only signal. The S7
# change removed "a security control whose state depends on which shell
# launched it"; that property was reachable again one FILE away, because
# NODE_ENV selects which env file Next loads.
# `loadRootEnv`'s NEVER_FROM_FILE does not help there (Next has its own
# loader), so the file must simply be untrackable. `.env.example` is the one
# exception and is tracked deliberately.
.env
.env.*
# Local development administrator's TOTP enrolment (otpauth URI + backup codes) — never committed.
.dev-admin.local.json
!.env.example

